{
  "axis_name": "Generative cognitive projection vs. Receptive systemic groundedness",
  "pos_pole": "This pole represents intense, self-directed mental activity that constructs and projects outward \u2014 generating new narratives, meanings, strategies, and identities through active cognitive elaboration. Concepts here involve building complexity from internal processes: reconstructing the self, creating original content, deconstructing hidden meanings, and imposing one's internal state onto the world through deliberate, focused intellectual or emotional energy.",
  "neg_pole": "This pole represents being anchored in external patterns, embodied responses, and systemic reality rather than generating from within. Concepts here involve reducing, reflecting, or mirroring what already exists \u2014 operating through instinct, physical sensation, natural equilibrium, or derivative copying rather than original cognitive construction. The orientation is toward receiving, simplifying, and responding to the world rather than actively reshaping it through mental projection.",
